      "description": "Watch Los Angeles FC vs Sporting Kansas City highlights and goals from Major League Soccer on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 26, 2026. A High-Stakes MLS Showdown On July 26, 2026, the pitch played host to an electrifying Major League Soccer clash between Los Angeles FC and Sporting Kansas City . The atmosphere was thick with anticipation as both sides looked to establish early dominance in a match characterized by tactical intensity and clinical attacking sequences. First-Half Momentum The intensity was evident from the start, with Heung-Min Son scoring in just the 5th minute to electrify the home crowd. Despite an early yellow card for Manu Garcia in the 2nd minute, the game remained a physical contest. LAFC found their rhythm as Denis Bouanga struck in the 37th minute, assisted by Mathieu Choiniere , before David Martinez added another goal in the 45+4 minute, courtesy of a Bouanga assist, sending the hosts into the break with a commanding lead. Second-Half Control As the second half unfolded, both managers utilized their benches to freshen up the squads. The visitors struggled to break down the resilient home defense, with frustrations mounting as Calvin Harris received a yellow card in the 75th minute. The final blow to any comeback hopes came in the 85th minute, when Denis Bouanga scored his second of the match, assisted by Tyler Boyd , ultimately putting the game out of reach before the final whistle blew in the 90+6 minute."
